From: Arjune <arjunevaibhavpatil1434@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] xen-kbdfront: present the absolute pointer as a touchscreen

QEMU's xenfb backend gives the guest an absolute pointer with mouse
buttons. Android's EventHub only classifies a single-touch device as a
touchscreen if it reports BTN_TOUCH, and only maps it to the display if
it has INPUT_PROP_DIRECT, so the Xen pointer was ignored.

In absolute mode, also advertise BTN_TOUCH and INPUT_PROP_DIRECT and
send BTN_TOUCH together with BTN_LEFT.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Android guest specific]
---
--- a/drivers/input/misc/xen-kbdfront.c	2026-10-25 10:07:41.344584090 +0530
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/xen-kbdfront.c	2026-10-25 10:07:41.379580692 +0530
@@ -98,6 +98,10 @@
 	}
 
 	input_event(dev, EV_KEY, key->keycode, value);
+	/* An absolute pointer is presented as a touchscreen: left = touch */
+	if (dev == info->ptr && key->keycode == BTN_LEFT &&
+	    test_bit(BTN_TOUCH, dev->keybit))
+		input_event(dev, EV_KEY, BTN_TOUCH, value);
 	input_sync(dev);
 }
 
@@ -288,6 +292,16 @@
 	for (i = BTN_LEFT; i <= BTN_TASK; i++)
 		__set_bit(i, ptr->keybit);
 
+	/*
+	 * Android only uses a single-touch device as a touchscreen if it has
+	 * BTN_TOUCH and INPUT_PROP_DIRECT; without them an absolute pointer
+	 * (e.g. QEMU's xenfb backend, driven over VNC) is ignored.
+	 */
+	if (abs) {
+		__set_bit(BTN_TOUCH, ptr->keybit);
+		__set_bit(INPUT_PROP_DIRECT, ptr->propbit);
+	}
+
 	ret = input_register_device(ptr);
 	if (ret) {
 		input_free_device(ptr);
